; savedelete.eval - a save that cannot be deleted says so (code-review C367).
; Judged by tools/WorldTest.py phase 22, which holds worldsaves_a OPEN for the
; length of the run (another process's handle, as a sync client or an editor
; would hold it) and has made worldsaves_b read-only.
;
; The row's Delete used to throw the error away, so the save just came back in
; the list with nothing said. `deletesave` is that row's own call: the read-only
; save goes (the library deletes past the attribute - the control that a
; delete works at all), and the open one is refused with the page's own line,
; the system's error code in it and its sentence in the log.
logecho on
reset
echo --- delete: a read-only save ---
deletesave worldsaves_b
echo --- delete: a save held open ---
expect-refuse deletesave worldsaves_a
